[{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q1","number":1,"question":"<p><strong>The following section requires the use of Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions and the Compound Angle Formulae.</strong></p><p>Sketch each of the following curves for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which are given in polar form:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=2\\sec\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\notin\\{\\frac\\pi2,\\frac{3\\pi}2\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=-6\\cosec\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\notin\\{0,\\pi,2\\pi\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=2\\sec\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad r\\cos\\theta=2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=-6\\cosec\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\frac{-6}{\\sin\\theta}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad r\\sin\\theta=-6.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Sketch each of the following curves in polar form for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Label the values at which they cross the coordinate axes.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=2\\sec(\\frac\\pi4-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\notin\\{\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{5\\pi}4\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=2\\cosec(\\frac\\pi4-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\notin\\{\\frac{3\\pi}4,\\frac{7\\pi}4\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=-3\\cosec(\\frac\\pi6-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\notin\\{\\frac\\pi6,\\frac{7\\pi}6\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=-4\\sec(\\frac{5\\pi}6-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\\notin\\{\\frac\\pi3,\\frac{4\\pi}3\\}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>From <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=2\\sec(\\frac\\pi4-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\cos(\\tfrac\\pi4-\\theta) =2,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\cos\\tfrac\\pi4\\cos\\theta+r\\sin\\tfrac\\pi4\\sin\\theta =2,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}{2}x+\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}{2}y =2,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny =-x+2\\sqrt2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>From <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=2\\cosec(\\frac\\pi4-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\sin(\\tfrac\\pi4-\\theta) =2,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\sin\\tfrac\\pi4\\cos\\theta-r\\cos\\tfrac\\pi4\\sin\\theta =2,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}{2}x-\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}{2}y =2,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny =x-2\\sqrt2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>From <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=-3\\cosec(\\frac\\pi6-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\sin(\\tfrac\\pi6-\\theta) =-3,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\tfrac12x-\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}y =-3,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny =\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{3}x+2\\sqrt3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>From <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=-4\\sec(\\frac{5\\pi}6-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\cos(\\tfrac{5\\pi}6-\\theta) =-4,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n-\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}x+\\tfrac12y =-4,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny =\\sqrt3x-8.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The following curves are of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=p\\sec(a-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;a&lt;\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. In each case find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <strong>a)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.51/questions/q3a_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p><strong>b)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.51/questions/q3b_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p><strong>c)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.51/questions/q3c_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The line has gradient <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=-6/(6/\\sqrt3)=-\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\sqrt3x-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=r\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=r\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr(\\sin\\theta+\\sqrt3\\cos\\theta)=-6.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The coefficient amplitude is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{1^2+(\\sqrt3)^2}=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, with phase <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi/6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sin\\theta+\\sqrt3\\cos\\theta=2\\cos(\\theta-\\tfrac\\pi6).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2r\\cos(\\theta-\\frac\\pi6)=-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and, since cosine is even,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\cos(\\tfrac\\pi6-\\theta)=-3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac\\pi6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The line has gradient <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=-8/(8\\sqrt3)=-\\sqrt3/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}x+8\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr(\\sin\\theta+\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{3}\\cos\\theta)=8\\sqrt3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The coefficient amplitude is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt3/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, with phase <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sin\\theta+\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{3}\\cos\\theta=\\tfrac{2\\sqrt3}{3}\\cos(\\theta-\\tfrac\\pi3).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2r\\cos(\\frac\\pi3-\\theta)=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\na=\\tfrac\\pi3,\\qquad p=4.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The line has gradient <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x+2\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr(\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta)=2\\sqrt2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The amplitude is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Taking the phase in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta=\\sqrt2\\cos(\\theta-\\tfrac{3\\pi}4).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\cos(\\frac{3\\pi}4-\\theta)=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\na=\\tfrac{3\\pi}4,\\qquad p=2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>The following curves are of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=p\\cosec(a-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;a&lt;\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. In each case find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <strong>a)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.51/questions/q4a_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p><strong>b)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.51/questions/q4b_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The line has gradient <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x-4\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr(\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta)=-4\\sqrt2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta=\\sqrt2\\sin(\\theta-\\frac\\pi4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sqrt2r\\sin(\\theta-\\tfrac\\pi4)=-4\\sqrt2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Using the oddness of sine,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\sin(\\tfrac\\pi4-\\theta)=4,\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The line has gradient <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\sqrt3/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}x+2\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr(\\sin\\theta+\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{3}\\cos\\theta)=2\\sqrt3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The coefficient amplitude is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt3/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, with phase <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\pi/6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sin\\theta+\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{3}\\cos\\theta=\\tfrac{2\\sqrt3}{3}\\sin(\\theta+\\tfrac\\pi6).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin(\\theta+\\frac\\pi6)=\\sin(\\frac{5\\pi}6-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\sin(\\tfrac{5\\pi}6-\\theta)=3.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{5\\pi}6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Sketch each of the following, given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\alpha&lt;\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=k\\sec(\\alpha-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=k\\cosec(\\alpha-\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Expanding the compound angle,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\cos(\\alpha-\\theta) =k,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\theta+r\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\theta =k,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx\\cos\\alpha+y\\sin\\alpha =k,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny =-\\frac{\\cos\\alpha}{\\sin\\alpha}x+\\frac{k}{\\sin\\alpha}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The printed working gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sin(\\alpha-\\theta) =k,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\theta-r\\cos\\alpha\\sin\\theta =k,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx\\sin\\alpha-y\\cos\\alpha =k.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=16\\cos2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for each of the following restrictions:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq\\theta\\leq\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{3\\pi}4\\leq\\theta\\leq\\frac{5\\pi}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{7\\pi}4\\leq\\theta\\leq2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=16\\cos2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, consider</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\pm4\\sqrt{\\cos2\\theta}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=16\\cos2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, consider</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\pm4\\sqrt{\\cos2\\theta}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=16\\cos2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, consider</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\pm4\\sqrt{\\cos2\\theta}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Sketch each of the following curves which are given in polar form. You may assume that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is restricted to only values for which the curve exists. In each case label a point which lies furthest from the pole with its value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=25\\sin2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=10\\cos3\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=12\\sin4\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=9\\sin6\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=14\\cos5\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=7\\sin5\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=25\\sin2\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\pm5\\sqrt{\\sin2\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=10\\cos3\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\pm\\sqrt{10\\cos3\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=12\\sin4\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\pm\\sqrt{12\\sin4\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=9\\sin6\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\pm3\\sqrt{\\sin6\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=14\\cos5\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\pm\\sqrt{14\\cos5\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=14\\cos5\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\pm\\sqrt{14\\cos5\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Find the polar curve which are equations of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=a\\cos p\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=b\\sin q\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b,p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive. Dashed lines represent where the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is negative. <strong>a)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.51/questions/q8a_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p><strong>b)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.51/questions/q8b_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p><strong>c)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.51/questions/q8c_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The curve is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=16\\cos4\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The curve is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=9\\sin3\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The curve is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=36\\cos5\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has polar equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=64\\sin3\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and is shown on the graph below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.51/questions/q9_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the Cartesian coordinates of the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the Cartesian coordinates of the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the points of intersection of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with a second curve given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=\\sqrt{32}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\pi&lt;\\theta\\leq\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answers in Cartesian form to two decimal places.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> occurs at the first maximum of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt{64\\sin3\\theta}=8\\sqrt{\\sin3\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\frac\\pi2\\div3=\\frac\\pi6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=8\\cos\\tfrac\\pi6=4\\sqrt3,\\qquad y=8\\sin\\tfrac\\pi6=4,\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(4\\sqrt3,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> occurs at the second maximum of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt{64\\sin3\\theta}=8\\sqrt{\\sin3\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\frac\\pi6+\\frac{2\\pi}3=\\frac{5\\pi}6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=8\\cos\\tfrac{5\\pi}6=-4\\sqrt3,\\qquad y=8\\sin\\tfrac{5\\pi}6=4,\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q=(-4\\sqrt3,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>At an intersection, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=32=64\\sin3\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin3\\theta=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\pi&lt;\\theta\\leq\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta\\in\\left\\{\\tfrac\\pi{18},\\tfrac{5\\pi}{18},\\tfrac{13\\pi}{18},\\tfrac{17\\pi}{18},\\tfrac{25\\pi}{18},\\tfrac{29\\pi}{18}\\right\\},\\qquad r=\\sqrt{32}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The Cartesian coordinates, to 2 d.p., are</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(5.57,0.98),\\ (3.64,4.33),\\ (-3.64,4.33),\\ (-5.57,0.98),\\ (-1.93,-5.32),\\ (1.93,-5.32).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.51-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is defined by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^2=16\\cos4\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\theta&lt;\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\theta&lt;\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which the curve exists.</p></li></ol><p>A second curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=4\\cos4\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\theta&lt;2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Describe two similarities and two differences between the curves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt{16\\cos4\\theta}=4\\sqrt{\\cos4\\theta}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. We want values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos4\\theta&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The printed intervals are</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta\\in(0,\\tfrac\\pi8)\\cap(\\tfrac{3\\pi}8,\\tfrac{5\\pi}8)\\cap(\\tfrac{7\\pi}8,\\pi).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Similarities: both curves pass through the axes at the same point; the maximum value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; both curves are symmetric about the axes. Differences: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has four petals while <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has eight; <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has loops created by negative values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; the petals of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are wider than those of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>; and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is continuous while <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is discontinuous.</p>"]}]